* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf

# Captured HTML fixtures are evidence, not source: they must round-trip
# byte-for-byte, exactly as the live server sent them. Under the "* text=auto"
# rule above they would be stored LF-only and checked out CRLF on Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) but LF on Linux CI - so the same fixture would hash
# differently in the two places, which matters here because this project
# hashes fixture-derived content (meaningfulContentHash) and pins golden
# parser output against it. "-text" disables all line-ending translation.
# Deliberately scoped to hr-ge only: applying it to jobs-ge's already-merged
# fixtures would rewrite their working-tree bytes and is out of Phase 1B's
# scope, though the same fix is recommended for them (see
# src/adapters/hr-ge/RECON_NOTES.md).
src/adapters/hr-ge/fixtures/** -text

# GitHub's Linguist ranks languages by byte count, so these fixtures decide how
# the repo is labelled: hr.ge's SSR pages embed a large ng-state island (one
# index page alone is 1.9 MB), and 9.1 MB of captured HTML across 13 files
# outweighed 0.7 MB of TypeScript across 144, reporting the project as 94% HTML.
# They are captured evidence, not source, so mark them vendored - excluded from
# the language stats and collapsed by default in diffs, which is wanted anyway
# for a 1.9 MB file. Purely presentational: unlike the "-text" rule above this
# changes no stored or checked-out bytes, which is why it can safely cover
# jobs-ge's already-merged fixtures too.
src/adapters/*/fixtures/** linguist-vendored
